from lesson_writer import author,CPP

def w(rel,purpose,steps,adapt,detail,exercise,limits,suite):
 def tests(l):return detail+' Evidence: '+l(CPP/'support'/('RawArchiveOracle.java' if suite=='raw_archive' else 'ArchiveCacheOracle.java'),'Java oracle')+', '+l(CPP/'support'/(suite+'.cpp'),'native harness')+', '+l(CPP/'tools'/(suite+'_differential.py'),'driver')+'. The inspected existing report records '+('613' if suite=='raw_archive' else '734')+' matching cases with zero failures for the complete suite. Generic ERROR/IO_ERROR categories do not prove all exact exception names/messages.'
 author('src/org/minima/database/'+rel+'.md',purpose,steps,adapt,tests,exercise,limits+' The counterpart remains partial and full parity not_verified.')
w('archive/RawArchiveInput','Reads a gzip-compressed raw archive incrementally and returns groups of at most 256 blocks for synchronization.',[
 'connect opens file, buffered, gzip and data-input layers. Read a MiniByte cascade-presence flag; when true, read the Cascade. Then read the declared block count as MiniNumber narrowed to int and reset totalAdded to zero.',
 'The Java method does not clear an existing cascade when a later connection has a false presence flag. Reconnection and partial-connect errors can therefore retain earlier state.',
 'getNextIBD creates a fresh result. If declared blocks remain, attach the cascade only when totalAdded is zero, then read up to 256 TxBlocks, incrementing the counter after each successful addition.',
 'Once totalAdded reaches totalFound, subsequent calls return empty IBD objects. A zero or negative declared count also yields no blocks and does not attach even a present cascade.',
 'A failed block read throws before returning the local batch; earlier successful reads in that batch may already have advanced totalAdded. Retrying is therefore not equivalent to rewinding.',
 'stop closes the nested Java stream layers. The API does not automatically validate every unread block or gzip trailer merely because the declared block count has been satisfied.'
], 'Native GzipInput reuses zlib raw inflate with explicit gzip header, CRC and size handling, deferring trailer validation to a subsequent read like the Java stream. A 64 KiB object buffer retries static deserialization only on EOF, removes consumed bytes after success or other errors, and preserves stream progression. This adapter is part of the behavior being tested, not just an interchangeable decompression call.',
 'The Java oracle creates actual raw block/cascade payloads. The driver gzip-compresses them and checks block counts 0/1/2/255/256/257/513, no/empty/nonempty cascade, exact/overstated/negative declarations, repeated next/stop/connect calls, missing files, object/gzip truncation, corrupted CRC, concatenated members and trailing junk. Returned batch size, cascade presence/hash and IBD hash are compared.',
 'With 257 declared blocks, how many blocks do the first three successful getNextIBD calls contain? Why can a corrupt trailer remain unnoticed if no additional decompressed bytes are requested?',
 'Passing these fixtures establishes selected incremental/error behavior, not atomic archive import or full chain acceptance. Native pre-connect/null errors and exact logging differ; failed batch recovery and all gzip header combinations need full review.','raw_archive')
w('archive/TxBlockDB','A synchronized in-memory index of TxBlock objects keyed by their TxPoW IDs, with parent lookup and height-based cleanup.',[
 'addTxBlock inserts or replaces the object under its current TxPoW ID. findTxBlock returns the stored object reference or null; it does not copy the block.',
 'getChildBlocks scans map values and selects blocks whose current parent-ID hex string exactly equals the requested string. Ordering follows ConcurrentHashMap enumeration rather than block height.',
 'clearOld retains blocks with block number greater than or equal to the minimum. It builds a new map keyed from each retained block’s current ID, then replaces the original map.',
 'This rebuilding can reindex a block whose mutable TxPoW changed its ID after insertion. Before cleanup the old key may still point to the changed object.',
 'clearAll empties the current map. Every public method is synchronized in Java, so each complete operation holds the object monitor.'
], 'C++ uses a mutex around complete operations and a shared JavaConcurrentMap of shared_ptr<TxBlock>. The optional parent query represents Java null equality returning no children. Reusing the map adapter preserves the tested collision/enumeration behavior and retaining pointers preserves row identity.',
 'The cache fixture creates deliberately colliding IDs, inserts duplicates, checks returned pointer identity, queries five parent groups, mutates every third TxPoW ID, cleans at thresholds -6/0/1/17/32 and checks reindexing and final clear. Sizes around collision thresholds and up to 256 exercise ordering and replacement.',
 'If a stored TxPoW ID changes from A to B, what can findTxBlock(A) and findTxBlock(B) return before and after clearOld retains that row?',
 'This is a cache, not an H2/MVStore replacement. Concurrent mutation of the TxBlock itself is separate from the cache mutex and remains outside the quiescent fixture.','archive_cache')
w('txpowdb/sql/TxPoWList','A serializable wrapper around a mutable list of TxPoW references, used when storing or transferring groups of proofs of work.',[
 'The public constructor stores the supplied ArrayList reference directly. Adding to that list afterward changes what the wrapper will serialize.',
 'Write a four-byte signed int count, followed by each TxPoW. This count is not encoded as MiniNumber, unlike many other Minima list formats.',
 'Reading immediately replaces the list, reads the signed count and appends complete decoded TxPoWs. A negative count executes zero loop iterations and leaves the rest of the input unread.',
 'If decoding fails partway through, the receiver retains the successfully appended prefix and the stream has advanced. The convenience converter instead returns null for IOException after logging it.',
 'The list can contain Java null through its public field/API, but serializing such an element fails; there is no add-method validation in this wrapper.'
], 'Native code uses shared_ptr<vector<shared_ptr<TxPoW>>> to preserve both the caller’s list alias and element references. A mutating read method replaces the shared list before reading the count and appends incrementally. The converter catches wire::IOException and logs through std::clog, with different diagnostic formatting from MinimaLogger.',
 'The make fixture constructs the wrapper before adding rows, directly testing caller-list aliasing. Lists of 0/1/2/5/17 objects include body-present and body-cleared TxPoWs. Derived reads compare bytes, consumed offset and retained list size for truncations, trailing bytes, negative counts and malformed nested objects; both direct read and convenience conversion are tested.',
 'Why would replacing the shared native list with a copied vector break the make fixture? What should remain in a receiver after the third TxPoW fails to decode?',
 'The wrapper’s package name does not mean these tests exercise SQL storage. Exact diagnostics, null-element errors and all alias lifetimes still need parity review.','archive_cache')
